# Who is asked to review a change (#247).
#
# One maintainer today, so every line names the same account; the lines exist so
# that the day a second maintainer joins, the sensitive paths can be given to
# whoever owns them without a hunt through the tree. Branch protection does not
# require a code-owner review (zero required approvals is a deliberate choice for
# one maintainer, recorded in the supply-chain decision, #247); this file makes sure review is *requested*.
# Later patterns win over earlier ones.

*                       @doancan

# What decides whether code can ship, and what it ships as.
/.github/               @doancan
/Dockerfile             @doancan
/docker/                @doancan
/docker-compose*.yml    @doancan
/scripts/               @doancan
/bun.lock               @doancan
/SECURITY.md            @doancan

# What decides who may see what.
/apps/api/src/platform/tenancy.ts   @doancan
/packages/db/migrations/            @doancan
